invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_mont64_addcarry.c
catches: rsa_addcarry_equiv_test
reason: block_mul_add drops the carry out of its chain, the carry from the
  four low words into the word above the block, so the word it returns is
  one short whenever that chain carries, which random words do about half
  the time. bin/rsa_addcarry_equiv_test runs the rows under any compiler
  and compares their words with rsa_mont64.c's loops.

--- old
    return (addcarry_word)(q3 >> 64) + carry;
--- new
    return (addcarry_word)(q3 >> 64) + (carry & 0);
